:name: csim RPL co-simulation
:description: Watch a live Contiki-NG RPL-UDP network from firmware running in Renode.
#
# Renode starts csim itself.  Setting simulationFilePath is what makes Renode
# open the two sockets, launch the peer with them on its command line, and
# shake hands — so run this from the csim checkout root and let it do the
# work:
#
#   make -C examples/renode/firmware       # once
#   renode examples/renode/csim-rpl.resc
#   (monitor) start
#
# The scenario csim runs comes from the environment, since Renode has no way
# to pass it through:  CSIM_CONFIG, CSIM_RENODE_FREQ_HZ (must match
# `frequency` in csim-host.repl — the tickClock message carries only a tick
# count), and optionally CSIM_LOG to keep csim's own output out of Renode's.
#
# Renode drives csim's clock from here on: every 1000 ticks of its 1 MHz
# clock it sends a tickClock and blocks until csim has simulated the same
# millisecond.  The timestamps the firmware prints are csim's simulation
# time, so its log lines up with csim's own.

$fw ?= @examples/renode/firmware/sniffer.elf
$launch ?= @tools/csim-renode-launch.sh

mach create "csim-host"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @examples/renode/csim-host.repl

showAnalyzer uart

csim SimulationFilePathMacOS $launch
csim SimulationFilePathLinux $launch

sysbus LoadELF $fw

echo ""
echo "csim window at 0x40100000, 1 ms quanta. 'start' to run, 'quit' to stop."
echo ""
